## Talk track — the short presentation

Use this sequence after setup. Allow about 12–15 minutes as a planning budget; model and evaluation latency varies. Open the completed comparison and final proof trace in advance. The detailed steps and complete setup inputs follow below.

| Beat | Show and do | Say | Check before moving on |
|---|---|---|---|
| Customer complaint | Open the linked disputed decision and its customer comment. | “The answer looks normal, but this customer says the financing decision is wrong. Let’s follow the evidence.” | Price, credit line and complaint belong to this application. |
| Investigation with Halo | Ask the neutral investigation question in step 2. Follow its retrieval and generation citations. | “The policy lookup found the amendment. Now compare that with the text the decision model actually received.” | The amendment is in retrieval; the compiled baseline input omits it. Keep generated history distinct from real calls. |
| Policy check | Open the Python evaluator, run the disputed and rejection samples, and inspect their amounts. | “We need to check the calculation as well as the decision. A correct rejection should pass.” | Five policy fields checked; no score is not a passing result. |
| Regression case | Ask Halo to prepare the reserved item, review its expectation, approve the single write and read it back. | “We keep the captured context and derive the expected result from the policy.” | Three string inputs, structured expectation, source links; {{ demo_dataset_items or 8 }} authored cases become {{ (demo_dataset_items or 8) + 1 }} after this single addition. If already curated, inspect it once. |
| Playground | Compare the same captured input with the two templates and identical model/schema/settings. | “The change adds the missing policy-updates binding. Everything else stays the same.” | Inspect grant and principal in both actual outputs. |
| Native experiments | Run or open both completed experiments on the frozen cohort. Show controls and full score coverage. | “Now we check the boundary cases too. In our completed rehearsal, four of nine passed before the change and all nine passed after it.” | Quote this run's actual counts; the nine-case result is rehearsal evidence, not a guarantee. |
| Promotion and monitoring | After the comparison, promote the tested version once, submit an eligible case and a PHEV control, then open their traces. | “The fresh decision records the version we tested. The policy check runs automatically on the agent, including correct rejections.” | Candidate version, actual amounts and automatic scores. If already promoted, use the recorded baseline and keep the current label. |

**Opening:** “A policy update can be available to an application and still never reach its decision model. We’ll investigate a customer complaint with Langfuse’s assistant, turn it into a regression case, test the prompt and verify a new decision.”

**Closing, after the checks pass:** “The complaint led us to the missing context. We preserved the case, tested the change against controls and verified the new version on fresh decisions.”

**If a live step is slow or unavailable:** state what is pending, then open the labelled completed rehearsal at the end of this runbook. Keep its project and execution date visible. Do not present a screenshot or predicted assistant answer as a new execution.

