### Recovery and evidence

- If Halo cannot read an object or perform an approved write, retain its answer and permission error. If a multi-item write becomes empty, inspect the current dataset and continue with reviewed single-item writes; never repeat an uncertain write blindly. Correct the project access or record the missing beat; a script-run action does not verify the integrated assistant.
- If a prompt variable is unresolved, reopen the saved item and restore all three string inputs. Use captured `metadata.prompt_variables`, not the compiled baseline user message.
- If a model output contradicts its amounts or contains multiple answers, retain the output as a failure. Do not repair it into a passing result.
- If a score is pending, inspect execution state and allow ingestion to settle. An execution error, missing score and false policy score are separate outcomes.
- Record every attempt in rehearsal, including five flagship comparisons per version and the genuine rejection controls. A retry does not replace an earlier failure. Record project/version, kit/core/SDK/model, dataset timestamp, prompt versions, settings, schema, rule/evaluator URLs and actual outputs. Link screenshots only after capturing those exact objects.

